      "question": "My manager wants a quick look at the oil condition on Transformer 1 at site MAIN. From the latest reading and the stats over the full available window, give me dielectric_rigidity, interfacial_v, oxygen, nitrogen and dbds, and say whether any of them moved in a direction that points to moisture ingress, air ingress or oil ageing. Rank the three concerns from most to least supported by the data. Don't use the combustible gases for this. If dielectric_rigidity or interfacial_v has no data, say so and base the ranking on oxygen and nitrogen only.",
      "answer": "**Transformer 1 (MAIN) – oil condition snapshot**\n\nData window: only 5 daily samples, 2024-01-15 → 2024-01-19 (latest reading is 2024-01-19, ~2.7 yrs old). All five parameters have data.\n\n| Parameter | Latest | Min | Max | Mean | Movement |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| dielectric_rigidity (kV) | 55 | 53 | 56 | 54.6 | Flat (first value also 55) |\n| interfacial_v (mN/m) | 45 | 44 | 46 | 45.0 | Flat |\n| oxygen (ppm) | 5,850 | 5,700 | 5,900 | 5,822 | Flat (first value 5,860) |\n| nitrogen (ppm) | 27,850 | 27,700 | 28,000 | 27,868 | Flat (first value 27,842) |\n| dbds (ppm) | 19 | 18 | 20 | 19.0 | Flat |\n\n**Directional assessment:** None of the five moved in a meaningful direction. Every latest value sits at or within ~1 σ of the window mean and matches the first sample, so there is no trend pointing to any of the three mechanisms. The judgement below rests on absolute levels, not movement.\n\n**Ranking (most → least supported):**\n\n1. **Air ingress** – weakly supported. O₂ ≈ 5.8k ppm and N₂ ≈ 28k ppm are moderate for a sealed unit (O₂/N₂ ≈ 0.21), so some atmospheric gas is present, but both are steady with no rising trend.\n2. **Oil ageing** – barely supported. Dielectric strength (55 kV) and IFT (45 mN/m) are healthy and flat, DBDS is stable at 19 ppm. Only the low O₂/N₂ ratio (<0.3) could hint at oxygen consumption by oxidation, and IFT doesn't corroborate it.\n3. **Moisture ingress** – not supported. Dielectric strength is high and steady; water_content is 0–1 ppm across the window.\n\n**Caveat:** five daily points is too short a window to detect trends; recommend comparing against older lab oil analyses before drawing conclusions.",
